# THE TEST KNOBS' MAP (2026-11-19): the prototype pathway the shipped map replaced, kept as the base the
# pad-0 test-course knobs (BZSHAPES, BZMAGNET, ... BZTURN: apps/bonanza/courses/path<knob>.sed) edit,
# each putting its course on pad 0 in FIRST's place.  Not shipped as the map: apps/bonanza/courses/path.bbc
# is (option A of docs/plans/bonanza-courses/pathway/).  First Roll and Little Hop have no pad here.
# Pad 1 is DOWN since 2026-11-21 (TRIAL's pad until TRIAL became a test course, SPEC.md 137.54; DOWN has its
# two exits), its icon still TRIAL's placeholder.
#
# The PATHWAY - BONANZA's map between courses (wave 8R, SPEC.md 137.22).
# A PROTOTYPE of today's six courses on two pages (the owner, 2026-11-16: a
# path screen; the map's final shape, 14 - 20 courses, is a later wave's).
# The marble AUTO-ROLLS along a route between glowing pads: finishing course
# A by exit E opens the one route keyed (A, E), whose gate sinks; an arrow
# on that route's side of the screen takes it, Enter plays the pad's course.
#
#   page 1 (above):   PEAK <-up-left-  MOON
#                                   ^ up (crosses into page 1)
#   page 0 (below):   MILL <-up- DOWN -right-> PLAY (a side pad; PLAY -up, left-> MILL, wave 8R round 2)
#                                   ^ up-right
#                                 FIRST (pad 0, where a new game rests)
#
# A screen direction is a ground step: +x down-right, -x up-left, +y
# down-left, -y up-right; both axes at once (equal amounts) down, up, left
# or right.  No secret route on the shipped map (--selfcheck tests one).
course PATH "The Pathway"
width  64
ball   rubber
pathway
music  fairway                              # (8b.10 gives the pathway its own)
rail   crystal                              # the route material (SPEC.md 137.22.8)
view   0 340                                # page 0's CGA window, centred at projection (0, 340)
pages  2
float  rect 0 0 64 64                       # the whole map FLOATS (the owner, 2026-11-16): crystal islands
                                            # with short icicle faces are the pathway's look (SPEC.md 137.27.2)

# pad N COURSE WX WY
pad 0 FIRST  22 26
pad 1 DOWN   22 21
pad 2 MILL   18 17
pad 3 PLAY   25 18
pad 4 MOON   13 12
pad 5 PEAK    7 12

# route A B exit E [secret] [gate WX WY] path WX,WY[,H] ...
route 0 1 exit 0  path 22,26 22,21                  # FIRST -> DOWN, up-right
route 1 2 exit 0  path 22,21 18,17                  # DOWN's exit 0 -> MILL, up
route 1 3 exit 1  path 22,21 25,18                  # DOWN's exit 1 -> PLAY, right
route 3 2 exit 0  path 25,18 25,17 18,17                  # PLAY -> MILL, up then left (R1: a player who took DOWN's exit 1 continues to MILL and so to MOON)
route 2 4 exit 0  path 18,17 13,12                  # MILL -> MOON, up, into page 1
route 4 5 exit 0  path 13,12 10,12 8,12,1 7,12,1    # MOON -> PEAK, up-left and up a ramp

# icon N FILE SX SY [fps F]: frame 0 the rest pose, the rest while the marble rests here
icon 0 icons/first.bba        -120 376
icon 1 icons/trial.bba         -88 328
icon 2 icons/mill.bba          -96 272
icon 3 icons/playground.bba     96 304
icon 4 icons/moon.bba           40 192
icon 5 icons/summit.bba       -104 104

# the lives, one counter a page
lives 29 22
lives 11  4
